  "description": "The checkpoint_threads head table (design/19-Async-Queryable-Store.md) is kept current by a trigger on checkpoints, whoever writes the log. Every SQL store in both engines inserts `inserts` into checkpoints as raw SQL, in order, then expects checkpoint_threads to hold exactly `threads` (by thread id). t-late's rows arrive out of order: the trigger must keep the higher sequence. Since design/29-Event-Waits-And-Timers.md the head also copies the row's wake_at (the innermost wait's, which the writer derives): t-waiting waits on a timer, and t-woken's timer was resumed, which keeps its wake_at but leaves it resumed, so not due. Since design/31-Graph-Identity.md it also copies the row's graph_id and graph_version (the outermost level's identity): t-identified was written by billing version 2, and t-unversioned by an unversioned graph.",
